# Git stores text as LF. Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` — which is set on Windows
# checkouts of this repo — materialises CRLF in the working tree, and Prettier's default
# `endOfLine: "lf"` then fails `format:check` on every file. Locally only: CI runs on
# Ubuntu where autocrlf is off, so the failure is invisible until someone clones on
# Windows and their first `pnpm check` reports 28 files of "code style issues" that are
# nothing but line endings.
#
# Normalising here keeps the working tree, the stored objects, and CI in step, and it
# overrides core.autocrlf regardless of how any individual machine is configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never line-ending-converted. SVG is deliberately absent — it is text,
# and Phase 2's placeholders under public/placeholders/ should normalise like any source.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
